# Milestone: M3
# Covers: nested tag-scope + try/finally cleanup ordering per row 7 §6.3;
#         verifies that the unwind walker pops TAG_SCOPE entries in innermost-
#         first order through nested scopes, executing each onleave body before
#         continuing outward.
#
# blocked: `onleave` keyword not yet supported — parse error (deferred-v1.x)
#   (T39 chk-driver reason stale; the chk driver uses urbi -i / urbi_repl_eval
#   which has always handled fork separators; the real blocker is `onleave`)
# matrix-row: tag-stop
#
# Reason (updated v0.13.4 probe):
#   The `onleave { ... }` clause is not yet parsed (deferred to v1.x per
#   language-compatibility-matrix).  Probing the source yields multiple
#   "expected expression" parse errors on the `onleave` keyword lines.
#   The nested try/finally ordering is already tested by
#   tests/chk/control_transfer/nested_finally.chk; this fixture must wait
#   for onleave parse/emit support.
#
# When M5 lands, implement this fixture by uncommenting the source below.
# Expected behaviour: log records cleanup in innermost-first order "ioIO".
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at M5):
#   var log = "";
#   var outer = Tag.new;
#   var inner = Tag.new;
#   try {
#     outer: {
#       try {
#         inner: { outer.stop() }
#           onleave { log = log + "i" }
#       } finally { log = log + "I" }
#     } onleave { log = log + "o" }
#   } finally { log = log + "O" };
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "ioIO"
